  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have an array AAA with NNN elements.\n\nYou can perform the following operation at most 20×N20 \\times N20×N times:\n\n\nSelect two indices i,ji, ji,j satisfying Ai≠AjA_i \\neq A_jAi​=Aj​, and set both AiA_iAi​ and AjA_jAj​ to Ai⊕AjA_i \\oplus A_jAi​⊕Aj​.\n\nHere, ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\nYour goal is to make the final array sorted in non-decreasing order. Find a sequence of operations that achieves this.\n\nIt can be proven that a solution always exists.\n\nNote that you don't have to minimize the number of operations.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN — the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, first print a single integer KKK, the number of operations you performed.\nThen, print KKK lines each containing two integers. The integers on the iii-th line should be the indices you selected for the iii-th operation.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "0≤Ai≤1090 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^90≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4\n34 40 20 30\n3\n1 2 3",
        "output": "2\n1 4\n1 3\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\nThe array becomes [60,40,20,60][60, 40, 20, 60][60,40,20,60] after the first operation. (Setting A1A_1A1​ and A4A_4A4​ to 34⊕3034 \\oplus 3034⊕30)\nThe array becomes [40,40,40,60][40, 40, 40, 60][40,40,40,60] after the second operation. (Setting A1A_1A1​ and A3A_3A3​ to 60⊕2060 \\oplus 2060⊕20)\n\nTest case 222:\n\nThe array is already sorted, so we don't need to perform any operations."
      }
    ]
  },
